From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Project Luma <builds@project-luma.local>
Date: Tue, 22 Sep 2026 20:30:00 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] luma: Dock icons can be rearranged

Dragging a dock icon to a new place never worked since the movable shelf
islands (0167): the drag started, no gap opened, and the icon snapped
back on release. Dragging a running app into the pinned apps was refused
the same way.

The work-area reservation for each shelf band is an invisible chrome
actor, stacked above the Shelf. A drag picks every actor under the
pointer, reactive or not, so the reservation was the drop target over
the whole band: it has no drop handling, the Dash was never asked, and
every drop was refused. The reservation is geometry only, so it is now
hidden from pick. Clicks were unaffected, which is why nothing else
showed it.

While an icon is dragged, the icon left in its place is dimmed to 35% at
its own size, the shared reorder feedback Filer's sidebar uses, instead
of growing: the lifted copy follows the pointer and the gap shows where
it will land.

Oracle: tests/gnome-shell/dock-reorder (reorder, pin by drag, persistence
across a restart, folders rail, arrange mode).
---
diff --git a/js/ui/dash.js b/js/ui/dash.js
index 6abc02b..a59c464 100644
--- a/js/ui/dash.js
+++ b/js/ui/dash.js
@@ -23,6 +23,8 @@ const SHELF_ITEM_ANIMATION_TIME = 160;
 const DASH_ITEM_LABEL_SHOW_TIME = 150;
 const DASH_ITEM_LABEL_HIDE_TIME = 100;
 const DASH_ITEM_HOVER_TIMEOUT = 300;
+// The icon a drag leaves behind: the shared reorder feedback's dimmed source.
+const DRAG_SOURCE_OPACITY = Math.round(0.35 * 255);
 
 export const DashIcon = GObject.registerClass(
 class DashIcon extends AppDisplay.AppIcon {
@@ -91,7 +93,9 @@ class DashIcon extends AppDisplay.AppIcon {
         const artwork = this.icon;
         artwork.set_pivot_point(0.5, 0.5);
         // Hover lifts the icon 2px and nothing else; a press dims it to 92%.
-        const scale = this._dragging ? 1.12 : 1;
+        // While it is dragged, the icon left in its place is the dimmed
+        // source of the shared reorder feedback, as in Filer's sidebar: the
+        // lifted copy follows the pointer and the gap shows where it lands.
         const lift = this.hover && !this._dragging ? 2 * St.ThemeContext.get_for_stage(global.stage).scale_factor : 0;
         let pressed = artwork.get_effect('luma-pressed');
         if (!pressed) {
@@ -104,7 +108,8 @@ class DashIcon extends AppDisplay.AppIcon {
         artwork.ease({
             translation_x: edge === 'left' ? lift : edge === 'right' ? -lift : 0,
             translation_y: edge === 'top' ? lift : edge === 'bottom' ? -lift : 0,
-            scale_x: scale, scale_y: scale,
+            scale_x: 1, scale_y: 1,
+            opacity: this._dragging ? DRAG_SOURCE_OPACITY : 255,
             duration: St.Settings.get().enable_animations ? 140 : 0,
             mode: Clutter.AnimationMode.EASE_OUT_QUAD,
         });
diff --git a/js/ui/shelf.js b/js/ui/shelf.js
index 15a0494..d0fcfbf 100644
--- a/js/ui/shelf.js
+++ b/js/ui/shelf.js
@@ -2469,6 +2469,13 @@ export const Shelf = GObject.registerClass({
             if (!actor) {
                 actor = new St.Widget({name: reservation.band ? 'lumaShelfWorkArea' : 'lumaDesktopEdgeInset',
                     reactive: false});
+                // A reservation is geometry for the work area and nothing
+                // else. It is chrome stacked above the Shelf, and a drag
+                // picks every actor, reactive or not: without this it is
+                // what a dragged dock icon lands on, which takes no drop,
+                // so reordering the dock and pinning by drag were refused
+                // with the pointer right over the icons.
+                Shell.util_set_hidden_from_pick(actor, true);
                 actor.connect('destroy', () => {
                     if (this._strutActors?.get(key) === actor)
                         this._strutActors.delete(key);
